# **Which pictures a changed path needs** (`Tools/gallery/render_affected.py`; owner, 2026-10-18: "哪怕是要跑，也不是每次都要
# full run，是不是？"). The gallery's and the UI tour's counterpart of Tools/e2e-affected.map. One rule a line:
#
#   <pattern>   <what...>
#
# <pattern> is a path from the repository's root, a shell pattern (`*` crosses `/`). **The first rule that matches
# decides**, so the specific come before the general. **The owner's rule (2026-10-18): renders run only when a
# dictionary's content style is being rectified, and only on that dictionary.** So: (a) a change confined to one
# dictionary (its role-table row, a style-ledger row of its) selects that dictionary's entries, light core, dark too
# only for colour; (b) a shared file (the reading style, the core's shared entry processing) selects one entry a
# dictionary, light core only (24), reason "shared file: reaches every dictionary"; (c) windows, menus, the popover and
# the page select UI-tour routes, no entry; (d) everything else, an unmatched path included, selects nothing, and
# `select` says so. FULL=1 alone gives the full gallery (288).
#
# <what> is `none` (no picture shows it), or any of:
#   rep                a shared file: one entry a dictionary (the `represent` kind of the gallery's keys)
#   profile            core/xdict-entry/src/roles/profiles.rs: the dictionaries of the role-table rows the diff's hunks
#                      touch, every gallery entry of theirs and their style-ledger repro entries; a hunk outside every
#                      row (the matcher, the types) is a shared change, `rep`
#   ledger             Tools/gallery/style-ledger.tsv: the dictionaries of the rows the hunks touch (a row's repro
#                      names one dictionary), their gallery and repro entries; dark too when the row is about colour
#   dict:<id>          every gallery entry of that dictionary
#   views:<set>        the views those entries are pictured in (a `viewset`); required beside an entry token
#   routes:<set>       the UI tour's routes of a `routeset`
#   route:<glob>       UI tour routes by id (Tools/ui-tour/routes.py), a shell pattern; each must match a route
#
#   dicts <id...>                  the test set (the 24): the gallery's keys are read for these alone
#   represent <kind>               the kind picturing a dictionary in `rep`
#   viewset <name> <view...>       views of the gallery (Sources/XDictEntryLab/Gallery.swift `modes`)
#   routeset <name> <glob...>      named route sets
#   profile <class> <id...>        a role-table row (its signature's first class) and the dictionaries in its markup
#   reads <view-glob> <path-glob...>   the style files a view reads: its render key's style inputs, exactly those its
#                                  lines name (so an edit to another invalidates none of its pictures)

dicts ahd cald ced cepd chambers cobuild cobuild-ec etym ldoce ldoce-ec lpd med mwaled mwc mwu noad oald oalecd ocd ode odecn oed peu yhdcd
represent long

viewset all   core-light core-dark coresans-light coresans-dark
viewset core  core-light

routeset panel  panel.* entry.find entry.zoomIn entry.collapse
routeset page   page.*
routeset search main.* search.* scope.* trail.* window.min
routeset menus  menu.* menubar.extra about acknowledgments

# Every row of core/xdict-entry/src/roles/profiles.rs `PROFILES`, by its signature's first class. Measured 2026-10-18
# by the class in the 24's own sheets on the build Mac, except cepd, cobuild-ec, noad and ocd, whose sheets are inside
# their .mdd: those are the row's own comment. render_affected.py fails while a row has no line here.
profile chwd           ldoce ldoce-ec
profile oup_icons      oald
profile odecn          odecn
profile dictentry      ced
profile di-head        cepd
profile cb13_jp        chambers
profile collins_en_cn  cobuild cobuild-ec
profile scnt           mwaled mwu
profile word__name     etym
profile boxsensefull   med
profile m1             noad
profile ocd_hw         ocd
profile a8e            ode
profile cxa            yhdcd
profile peu-quote      peu

# The four views read the column and type layers alike (`EntryReadingFrame.all` and `[.column, .type, .sans]`); the
# minimal frame's files are "Original style"'s only, which no view of the four draws.
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/appearance.js apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/colour-*.js
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/column.css apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/controls.css
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/marks.css apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/reading-labels.css
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/type.css apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/frame*.js
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/disclosure*.js apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/pron-run*.js
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/find*.js apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/readability-core.js
reads *  apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/placeholder-clicks.js apps/apple/Sources/XDictEntryView/Style/speaker-clicks.js

# --- What no picture shows, named so `select` does not list it as unmatched --------------------------------------------
